## Why This Is Asked
This tests a practical beginner-friendly AWS DVA pipeline across regions, with client-side pre-validation, per-record quality scoring, deduplication, and clear routing of valid/invalid data. It also touches backfill planning and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Client-side validation to reduce cloud load
- Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, DynamoDB for dedupe
- S3 Parquet partitioning by region/date
- DLQ routing for invalids
- Backfill planning and CloudWatch observability
- LocalStack testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example snippet
function validate(rec) {
  const ok = rec && typeof rec === 'object' && typeof rec.deviceId === 'string' && typeof rec.ts === 'number';
  if (!ok) return false;
  const { temp, humidity } = rec;
  return (temp >= -50 && temp <= 150) && (humidity >= 0 && humidity <= 100);
}
